## Why This Is Asked
Tests real-world idempotency handling, crucial for payment-like APIs.

## Key Concepts
- Idempotency keys per tenant; per-tenant isolation; race-condition handling; retry semantics; error handling.

## Code Example
```javascript
// pseudocode: idempotency guard
if (exists(tenantId, idempotencyKey)) return cachedResponse;
beginTxn();
if (exists(tenantId, idempotencyKey)) return cachedResponse; // double-check
order = createOrder(payload);
cache(tenantId, idempotencyKey, order);
commitTxn();
return order;
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test with network hiccups causing duplicate Idempotency-Key submissions?
- How would you monitor and alert on idempotency violations?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests must reflect production-like data flow, multi-tenant isolation, and dynamic policy propagation. This question probes end-to-end observability, concurrency control, and resilience under partial outages.

## Key Concepts
- End-to-end quota enforcement across multi-node deployments
- Real-time streaming integrity (order, dedup, latency)
- Propagation of dynamic admin-configured quotas (fast consistency)
- Failure modes: Redis/Kafka outages, partial consumer lag

## Code Example
```javascript
